<section class="studio-pillars section-space"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">The things we come back to</p><div class="pillar-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">01 / Clay</p><h3>A grounded beginning.</h3><p>We imagine working with stoneware for its substance and quiet strength. The starting point is always how the material feels, and what it asks of a form.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">02 / Glaze</p><h3>Room for variation.</h3><p>A glaze can pool, break, soften, and surprise. Test tiles and patient notes help us understand those changes without sanding away their character.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">03 / Pace</p><h3>Time is a material.</h3><p>Drying and firing cannot be hurried without consequence. Making in small groups allows time for each stage and a closer look at every result.</p></article></div></div></section>
